course: dictionary
lesson: 2439
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is right. Dairy can mean food made from milk, a place where milk is made into butter or cheese, or a small corner shop in New Zealand.
explain: Look at the words near it. «From the farm the milk travels cold in a tanker to the dairy, where a quick heating called pasteurisation kills the germs.» The milk is heated at this place, so dairy means the place where milk is made into products.
explain: «The other parts are protein foods such as beans, eggs, fish and meat, dairy or alternatives.» Dairy sits in a list with eggs and meat, which are foods, so here dairy means food made from milk, such as cheese, butter and yoghurt.
explain: When a word can mean several things, try each meaning in the sentence and keep the one that makes sense. Dairy can also be an adjective that describes a noun, as in «dairy cows», which are cows related to milk.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: As a noun, «dairy» can mean food made from milk, such as cheese, butter, yoghurt and cream.
fact: «Dairy» can also mean a place where milk is kept and made into butter or cheese.
fact: In New Zealand, «pop down to the dairy» means go to a small corner shop, often for sweets.
fact: As an adjective, «dairy» means related to milk, as in «dairy farm» or «dairy cows».
exercise: «The other parts are protein foods such as beans, eggs, fish and meat, dairy or alternatives.» What does dairy mean here? | A small corner shop | *Food made from milk, such as cheese and yoghurt | A place where milk is made into butter | A tanker that carries milk
exercise: A New Zealand child says, «Pop down to the dairy for some lollies.» What is a dairy here? | *A small corner shop | A farm where cows are milked | A big supermarket with a dairy aisle
exercise: In «dairy cows», what does dairy describe? | The milk tanker | The farm where the cows live | *The cows, as related to milk | The sweets the children buy
test: «Starchy food is great fuel, but the body also needs protein, fruit and veg, dairy and some fats.» What does dairy mean here, and what kind of word is it? | A noun: a small corner shop | *A noun: food made from milk | An adjective: related to milk | A noun: a place where milk is kept
test: «A dairy cow can give 25 to 30 litres a day, and today many are milked by machines.» In this sentence, what kind of word is dairy? | *An adjective, describing the cow | A noun meaning a place | A verb meaning to milk | A noun meaning a shop
exam: Which sentence uses dairy to mean a place where milk is made into butter or cheese? | Dairy cows can give 25 to 30 litres a day | *The milk travels cold in a tanker to the dairy | Dairy or alternatives are protein foods | Starchy food is great fuel
